# MyYouTube agent rules

## Scope

- This repo is **MyYouTube** — a standalone personal YouTube client (Electron + React).
- **Do not** reference, import, copy from, or depend on any other project (including any file manager or training apps).
- Canonical plan: `PLAN.md`. Specs: `docs/`. Implement against those files only.

## Architecture

- Electron **main** owns: OAuth token vault, YouTube Data API calls, SQLite, sync, feed aggregation, recommendation scoring, settings persistence.
- Renderer is React + Zustand; **no Node integration**.
- Typed preload IPC + Zod; Result envelope `{ ok, value } | { ok: false, error }`.
- App state only under Electron `userData` — never write personal DB/tokens into the repo or arbitrary folders.
- Playback only via **official YouTube IFrame Player** (or supported embed). No stream-URL extraction.

## Product locks

- Subscription feed must never silently include discovery / injected recommendations.
- No autoplay or infinite scroll by default; prefer pagination / Load more.
- Explicit interests dominate behavioural inference.
- Recommendation scores must be explainable (store components).
- MVP ships **without** AI/embeddings; keep classifiers behind an interface later.

## YouTube / security

- Use YouTube Data API v3 + Google OAuth only; no scraping youtube.com for API-covered data.
- Never commit `.env`, client secrets, tokens, or `*.sqlite` user databases.
- Do not log access/refresh tokens.
- Verify current Google/YouTube API docs and ToS before implementing API calls.

## Specs vs code

Until scaffold exists, prefer updating `docs/` + `PLAN.md` when product decisions change; then implement.
Keep [docs/DECISIONS.md](docs/DECISIONS.md) in sync when locking behaviour.
